{
  "//": "Lineage: the registry of Craft apps. Written by hand, except each app's upstream block, which `mise run apps:fetch` rewrites from GitHub (docs_port is the port the app's own docs use in examples). Read by mise-tasks/gen, which generates mise.toml, .mcp.json and mcp-live.json from it, and by mise-tasks/status. An app with an mcp block is checked end to end. Its mcp fields: port; live, the args that drive the running app ({port} stands for mcp.port); headless, extra args for the headless server; opens_itself; usage, the CLI's own mcp usage line; opens_with, what a freshly opened app holds, and first_step, the tool call to make before working when it holds nothing to work on; live_only_tools, tools only the live server has; look, the tools for seeing the result; file_roots, whether the CLI can confine the agent's file access with --automation-read-root / --automation-write-root (this repo passes neither); control_token, where the app keeps its control token. limits are things that go wrong; notes are other things worth knowing.",
  "apps": [
    {
      "id": "cadcraft",
      "name": "CADCraft",
      "repo": "storytold/cadcraft",
      "version": "0.13.0",
      "install": {
        "cli": "cadcraft-cli-*-macos-universal.zip",
        "cli_bin": "cadcraft-cli",
        "app": "cadcraft-*-macos-universal.dmg"
      },
      "bundle": {
        "name": "CADCraft.app",
        "executable": "CADCraft"
      },
      "mcp": {
        "port": 7979,
        "live": [
          "--connect",
          "127.0.0.1:{port}",
          "--lazy",
          "--launch"
        ],
        "opens_itself": true,
        "usage": "cadcraft-cli mcp [--connect HOST:PORT [--lazy] [--launch]]",
        "opens_with": "a new drawing",
        "live_only_tools": [
          "screenshot",
          "ui_click",
          "ui_inspect"
        ],
        "look": [
          "render"
        ],
        "file_roots": false,
        "control_token": "~/.cache/cadcraft-control-{port}.token"
      },
      "checked": {
        "version": "0.13.0",
        "on": "2026-10-26"
      },
      "limits": [
        "The first live call right after --launch opens the app can fail with 'missing or invalid control token': the bridge reads the old token before the app writes a new one (upstream #2087). The error says it is safe to send again, and the retry works."
      ],
      "notes": [
        "--launch opens the app with `open -a CADCraft`, which only finds the copy mise installed because scripts/unpack-dmg.sh registers it with macOS."
      ],
      "upstream": {
        "about": "CADCraft: computer-aided design and drafting — an open-source, clean-room AutoCAD-style app in pure Rust",
        "latest": "0.13.0",
        "docs": "https://github.com/storytold/cadcraft/blob/main/docs/mcp.md",
        "docs_port": 7979,
        "cli_platforms": [
          "macos-universal"
        ],
        "app_platforms": [
          "freebsd-x86_64",
          "linux-aarch64",
          "linux-riscv64",
          "linux-x86_64",
          "macos-universal",
          "windows-arm64",
          "windows-x64",
          "windows-x86"
        ]
      }
    },
